{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"store"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ids"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"deleted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID"},{"kind":"text","text":"> = [], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","text":"MergePolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The live store to reconcile."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"store"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The identities to re-read. IDs matching no row, and IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"belonging to another entity type, are harmless."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"ids"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identities known to have been deleted elsewhere."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"deleted"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"policy"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The O(k) counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", which re-reads every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of every registered entity on every tick. Where a sync signal carries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" identities changed, this spends that knowledge: one batched fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per 500 IDs instead of a full-table scan, and only the named entities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconciled. Everything else in state is left exactly as it was.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every guarantee ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" makes holds here. Pending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes are flushed first; an ID with unflushed local intent — a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drained-but-unflushed write, an un-drained edit, a pending deletion, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write whose save failed, or an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","type":"reference"},{"text":" hold — always wins, and that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not configurable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A partial read cannot tell a deleted row from one that was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never asked about, so this "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" infers a deletion. An ID vanishes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only if you name it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"type":"text","text":", and only if the resolved policy grants"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/removesMissingEntities","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Name only what you have positive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evidence for — a history tombstone, not an empty fetch. In exchange,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"there is no empty-snapshot guard to work around: this can remove the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last surviving entity, which "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" cannot."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ID named in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"text":" that storage ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"still holds"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is not removed. A live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row is evidence the deletion was itself undone elsewhere; a tombstone can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be stale.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Deferred rows are re-offered","anchor":"Deferred-rows-are-re-offered","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tick may read a row and decline to apply it — an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","type":"reference"},{"text":" hold is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exemption that leaves no other trace. Those rows are remembered by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity and re-offered on the next call, on top of whatever ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ids"},{"text":" names,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a caller does not have to re-queue them against its own signal. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matters here because a sync signal is generally not resent and releasing a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hold writes no transaction of its own, so without it a hold would quietly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"become a veto. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" shares the same debt, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either path settles what the other deferred. Both discard it when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"container is swapped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Registered ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse:"},{"text":" resolvers do not run here — a resolver is handed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole table and asked which rows survive, and a subset would have it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"judge a world it cannot see. Duplicate rows are still collapsed on read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and still reported. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapseDuplicates(into:)-(Store)"},{"text":" or a full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" to reclaim them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","title":"mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0B11CoordinatorCAA0A00A10ObservableRzrlE11mergeRemote4into3ids7deleted6policyyAD5StoreCyxq_G_Shy10Foundation4UUIDVGAqA11MergePolicyVSgtYaF","symbolKind":"method","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Store","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ids"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Set","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"deleted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Set","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MergePolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Re-hydration restricted to the rows a caller already knows changed.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergeremote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistenceCoordinator/mergeChanges(into:policy:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergechanges(into:policy:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)","role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"title":"mergeChanges(into:policy:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Merges only the rows persistent history says changed, falling back to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistenc